's many people like that that  just don't want it but there may be some  that are like that and that's a person  and that's a personal choice to them you  know if you decide to have a vaccine put  into your body of course we have lots of  vaccines for different things at the  moment and that's a personal choice to  them I don't think it's selfish what  politicians should be doing and what I'm  doing is encouraging people to speak to  their doctor if they've got concerns  about the vaccine get the right  information not stuff online that may be  not factually correct but actually speak  to your GP speak to the medical experts  and get the vaccine I got the vaccine I  thought it was safe for me and that was  a personal choice but I don't think I  should be then preaching to other people  about what choices are it is the wrong  decision if you choose not to have a  vaccine for no other reason than you  either don't you know you don't want to  do it for whatever reason that might be  that is not  um that is not presumably what your  party would stand for because you want  all of us to look after each other  that's the social thing to do it is and  we're of course encouraging people to  take the vaccine but even after you've  had the vaccine you can still get the  virus it's not 100  um you know immunity to the virus so  that's why we're saying testing is an  important part of that and of course  making sure that if you're in an  occupational workplace that you have the  appropriate equipment to keep you safe  that this ventilation where possible and  the government have failed to do enough  on that you know we've got the scores  going back in September we should be  putting proper ventilation into those  schools so that we can follow the sage  advice and make sure that we're doing  everything we possibly can to keep  control of the virus uh what's Labor  doing to honor victims of the child sex  abuse of care home residents from the  60s to the 90s in London it's absolutely  appalling that what we've seen in  Lambeth over that period and the  children that suffered so badly over  that period is absolutely heartbreaking  the most things that we need to do is  first of all recognize the failures that  happened over you know decades in  Lambeth and then learn from those  mistakes we've seen this in other parts  of the country and that actually have to  recognize where this predatory behavior  has happened and where people are in  positions of authority have failed those  young people so badly and you know my I  feel so strongly about this because  often often it's vulnerable people from  backgrounds like my own that have been  put into situations where they should  have been kept safe and the system has  completely failed them we have to learn  the lessons of that and part of that is  recognizing where we did things wrong  and then making sure that that can never  happen again before I let you go John  Butler um thrown out of the uh chamber  for saying that the Prime Minister was a  liar we had Annie McDonald on from your  party yesterday saying what he is a liar  I put that to the work and pension  secretary this morning she said he's  more popular than your leader  well I mean I just think that you know  Don Butler was correct and it's it's  absolutely ludicrous that if somebody's  lied especially the prime minister of  this country that you can't call that  out in Parliament it's our uh archaic  way of doing things in Parliament but if  somebody's lied I think you should be  able to if you could back that up and  show that that person has lied then we  should be able to say that and that but  it was quite right to say that why then  do you think he's more popular than your  leader why do you think he's the Prime  Minister well British people trust him  more than they trust your leader well I  think that care is doing a fantastic job  as being the leader of the opposition  it's been difficult times but I actually  do think that we're going ahead now  we're showing people that we're a  government in waiting like the policy  that I've announced today around  flexible working this government is  running out of tract and on their lies  their corruption and their and their  Bluster we've seen this Bluster you know  you can't keep blustering forever there  has to come a point where you actually  do what you say and that's not what the  government have been doing so I think  there's going to be a Day of Reckoning  for Boris it's great to see you thanks  for coming in thank you really  appreciate it thank you

